Arkansas State Police are looking for  the cause of a bus crash that killed a  nine-year-old boy nearly 50 passengers  most of them children were hurt when the  charter bus flipped Monday morning on  Interstate 30 near Little Rock it was  taking youth football players home to  Memphis after a championship tournament  in Dallas  Omar Villafranca is in Little Rock Omar  good morning good morning we learned the  bus drivers name is EULA Jarrett and  that most of the passengers on her bus  were in elementary school there's still  four kids here at Arkansas Children's  Hospital and one of the passengers on  the bus told us he felt the bus swerved  and then violently rolled I woke up when  I liked a lot of screaming and the  coaches were trying to keep everybody  calm  tied jeer Terrell is one of at least 26  children some he says as young as six  years old who were injured when their  charter bus ran off this highway ramp  the 13-year old walked away with 18  stitches in his head and a bruise around  his left eye so he under side thought I  was gonna die and we lost one the crash  killed nine year old Cameron Johnson  Taiji's mother Deidre Terrell used to  take care of Cameron he was a joy dr.  Todd Maxon says the flood of patients  filled the ER at Arkansas Children's  Hospital the injuries have ranged really  from injuries to the skull and brain to  lots of lacerations lots of broken bones  Arkansas State Police say the bus driver  told them she lost control of the  vehicle causing it to roll the charter  bus company that owns the bus  tennessee-based scott shuttle service  received federal regulators highest  safety rating the business was fined in  July for allowing the driver to operate  one of its vehicles without a proper  license a lot of them never had the  opportunity to leave Memphis JT Bragg  oov is one of several coaches and  parents who raised over a hundred miles  from Memphis to Little Rock to help care  for the injured children it was a huge  trip for these kids in the  a complete tragedy the bus company has  not responded to our request for  comments we don't know if there were  seatbelts on the bus but we do know  there was a black box and that's where  investigators hope to learn a little bit  more about the crash as for the four  kids still at the hospital doctors say  they're expected to make a full recovery  John Omar thank you
 

